INSERT OR IGNORE INTO stories (id, slug, lane, type, section_slug, status, sensitive, headline, dek, body, byline, hero_image_url, hero_image_credit, hero_image_rights, source_system, source_ref, priority, is_lead_candidate, created_by, created_at, updated_at) VALUES ('bd-20261018-boston-winter-guide', 'things-to-do-boston-fall-winter-2026-holiday-events-guide', 'newsroom', 'feature', 'lifestyle', 'EDITORIAL_REVIEW', 0, 'Things to do in Boston this fall and winter 2026: a local''s guide', 'From the Boston Common tree lighting to Frostival''s drone shows and Copley lodge, here is what official calendars list for November through February.', 'Boston''s cold-weather calendar runs from neighborhood tree lightings in late November to a new winter lodge in Copley Square and a Ferris wheel on the Greenway in February. Many of the signature events are free, and nearly all of them sit within a short walk of an MBTA station. This guide draws only on schedules posted by the City of Boston, Meet Boston, the state tourism office, the National Park Service and the MBTA.

## What are the best free holiday events in Boston?

The city''s Parks and Recreation Department runs a string of free lighting ceremonies, and the City of Boston has posted 2026 dates for several of them.

- **Boston''s official holiday tree arrival (Nov. 24):** The tree from Nova Scotia is scheduled to arrive on Boston Common by police escort at about 11 a.m. The city says this is the 55th year of the gift, which honors Boston''s aid after the 1917 Halifax explosion.
- **Copley Square tree lighting (Nov. 30, 5–6 p.m.):** This year''s event doubles as the grand reopening of the renovated Copley Square Park, with a guided tour, crafts, Santa and performances, according to the city.
- **Boston Common tree lighting (Dec. 3, 6–8 p.m.):** Held near the Visitor Information Center at 139 Tremont St. The city lists Mayor Michelle Wu and Nova Scotia Premier Tim Houston as participants.
- **Commonwealth Avenue Mall lighting (Dec. 3, about 8 p.m.):** Right after the Common ceremony, lights go on along the mall from Arlington Street to Charlesgate, a project the city runs with the Friends of the Public Garden.

The city''s events page also lists a trellis lighting at Christopher Columbus Park on Nov. 23 and the lighting of the ship at Martin''s Park on Nov. 28.

## What is Boston Frostival?

Frostival is Meet Boston''s winter program, now in its second year. The tourism bureau announced the 2026-27 lineup in early October.

- **Holiday drone shows:** Over Boston Common on Saturdays, Dec. 5, 12 and 19, with two 15-minute shows each night at 6 and 8 p.m.
- **Frostival Lodge in Copley Square:** Opens Jan. 22 and runs through the end of February. Meet Boston says returning features include trivia, bingo, live music, games and NFL and NBA broadcasts, with tea service, wine tastings, a full bar and literary events added this year.
- **Ferris wheel on the Rose Kennedy Greenway:** A 75-foot wheel opens in February and runs through April 25. Meet Boston has not announced an exact opening day.

## What''s happening month by month this winter?

The table below lists events whose dates or recurring timing appear on official pages. Where a 2026-27 date was not yet posted, we say so.

| Month | Event | Where | Date or timing (per official source) |
|---|---|---|---|
| November | Trellis lighting | Christopher Columbus Park | Nov. 23 (City of Boston) |
| November | Official holiday tree arrival | Boston Common | Nov. 24, about 11 a.m. (City of Boston) |
| November | Lighting of the ship | Martin''s Park | Nov. 28 (City of Boston) |
| November | Copley Square tree lighting and park reopening | Copley Square | Nov. 30, 5–6 p.m. (City of Boston) |
| December | Boston Common tree lighting | Boston Common | Dec. 3, 6–8 p.m. (City of Boston) |
| December | Commonwealth Avenue Mall lighting | Back Bay | Dec. 3, about 8 p.m. (City of Boston) |
| December | Frostival drone shows | Boston Common | Dec. 5, 12, 19 at 6 and 8 p.m. (Meet Boston) |
| December | First Night Boston | Downtown | New Year''s celebration held since 1976; 2026-27 schedule not yet posted on the page reviewed (Meet Boston) |
| January | Frostival Lodge opens | Copley Square | Jan. 22 through end of February (Meet Boston) |
| February | Greenway Ferris wheel opens | Rose Kennedy Greenway | February through April 25 (Meet Boston) |
| February | Children''s Winter Festival | See City of Boston for 2027 site | Usually during Boston Public Schools February break; 2027 date not yet posted (City of Boston) |

All City of Boston lighting events listed above are free, according to the city''s event pages.

## What other holiday traditions do locals recommend?

Meet Boston''s holiday bucket list, last updated in December 2025, points to a set of annual favorites. The bureau had not posted 2026 dates for these on the page we reviewed, so check each venue directly.

- The Holiday Pops at Symphony Hall
- Boston Ballet''s "The Nutcracker"
- "Black Nativity"
- Ice skating at the Frog Pond on Boston Common
- Pop-up markets including the SoWa Winter Festival and the Holiday Market at Snowport
- Window-shopping on Newbury Street and Charles Street, and at the Prudential Center and Copley Place
- Bruins and Celtics games at TD Garden

For a cold-weather break, the same list suggests the Museum of Fine Arts, the Isabella Stewart Gardner Museum and the Museum of Science.

## Is the Freedom Trail open in winter?

Yes. The National Park Service says most sites in Boston National Historical Park stay open year-round, but hours change by season, with peak season generally running May through October. The park cautions that hours can shift for maintenance or weather.

A few practical notes from the park''s hours page, last updated Oct. 14, 2026:

- The Charlestown Navy Yard grounds are open around the clock, every day.
- Visitors 18 and older may need a valid federal or state photo ID to board USS Constitution.
- Old North Church lists a Discovery Pass at $10 for adults and $5 for children 6 to 12, with a bell chamber tour option at $15 and $10.
- The park recommends checking its alerts page or calling 617-242-5601 before visiting.

## How do I get around Boston in winter without a car?

The MBTA''s visitor guide makes the T the simplest option for most of the events above. Riders can tap a contactless credit or debit card, phone or watch at fare gates and on buses, or use a CharlieCard or CharlieTicket.

| Fare type (per MBTA visitor guide) | Price |
|---|---|
| Subway, one way | $2.40 |
| Local bus, one way | $1.70 |
| 1-day LinkPass (subway and local bus) | $11.00 |
| 7-day LinkPass (subway and local bus) | $22.50 |
| Commuter Rail weekend pass | $10.00 |
| Children 11 and under | Free |

The MBTA recommends confirming current fares on mbta.com before you travel.

Useful stops, according to the MBTA:

- **Boston Common and the Public Garden:** Park Street (Red and Green lines) or Boylston (Green Line).
- **Freedom Trail:** Park Street, State, Government Center, Haymarket and North Station; the Inner Harbor ferry reaches the Charlestown Navy Yard.
- **Faneuil Hall:** A short walk from Aquarium, Haymarket or Government Center.
- **From Logan Airport:** The SL1 bus is free and connects to the Red Line at South Station, with a free transfer.

## Are there winter day trips from Boston?

The Massachusetts Office of Travel and Tourism highlights a handful of winter festivals around the state. Its most recent roundup covered the 2025 season, so 2027 dates may differ. Events it featured include Salem''s So Sweet Chocolate and Ice Sculpture Festival, the Greenfield Winter Carnival, the Downtown Worcester Winter Festival and the Yarmouth Winter Carnival on Cape Cod, all typically held in late January or February.

## Frequently asked questions

### When is the Boston Common tree lighting in 2026?

The City of Boston lists the Boston Common tree lighting for Thursday, Dec. 3, 2026, from 6 to 8 p.m. The event is free and takes place near the Visitor Information Center at 139 Tremont St. The Commonwealth Avenue Mall lights are switched on immediately afterward.

### Why does Nova Scotia send Boston a Christmas tree?

The tree is a thank-you for the relief Boston sent after the 1917 Halifax Harbor explosion, according to the city. This year marks the 55th annual tree, and the first was donated in 1971.

### When are the Boston Frostival drone shows?

Meet Boston says the drone shows will run over Boston Common on Saturdays, Dec. 5, 12 and 19. Each night includes two 15-minute shows, at 6 p.m. and 8 p.m.

### When does the Frostival Lodge open in Copley Square?

Meet Boston says the lodge opens Friday, Jan. 22, and stays open through the end of February. Programming includes trivia, live music, sports broadcasts and new wine and tea events.

### Can I visit Freedom Trail sites in the winter?

Most Boston National Historical Park sites are open year-round, according to the National Park Service, though hours are shorter outside the May–October peak. Check the park''s alerts page or call 617-242-5601 for current hours.

### What is the easiest way to pay for the T as a visitor?

The MBTA lets riders tap a contactless bank card, phone or smartwatch on buses, subways and the Mattapan Trolley. A one-way subway ride is $2.40, and a 7-day LinkPass is $22.50, according to the MBTA''s visitor guide.', 'Boston Daily Staff', 'https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/6/6c/Trinity_Church,_Boston,_Massachusetts_LCCN2011630431.jpg/1280px-Trinity_Church,_Boston,_Massachusetts_LCCN2011630431.jpg', 'Photo: Carol M. Highsmith / Wikimedia Commons, public domain', 'public_domain', 'newsroom', 'content/2026-10-18-guides-long.sql', 6, 0, 'newsroom-assistant', '2026-10-18T19:30:00.000Z', '2026-10-18T19:30:00.000Z');
